@flexiarg translation/route-the-untranslatable
@title Refuse What Cannot Be Translated, And Route It With The Reason
@keywords refusal, untranslatable, routing, coverage, unwarranted
@audience translators, coordinators, coverage reporters
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-16 (claude-7; shared by test-registry, contracts and pattern-interpretation)
@references [pattern-interpretation/route-the-untranslatable test-registry/warrant-rides-the-handoff contracts/holder-states-the-claim hygiene/route-to-who-can-act]
@see-also translation/declare-what-is-lost
@why some units cannot cross under the declared preservation target: a run with no warrant, a function that disagrees with the Lean on an input class, a pattern whose clause no admitted fact expresses. Substituting a default or dropping the unit produces a translation of something else.
@how refuse with a typed reason naming the part that failed; route the refusal to whoever can act (the reviewer lane that reruns, the owner who aligns the runtime, authoring for the pattern); count refusals by cause, separating "cannot cross under the current rule" from "not translated yet".
@violation-signature an :unwarranted handoff silently rerun or silently trusted; a lagging correspondence not declared; a cascade scored with an uninterpreted pattern dropped.
! conclusion: Untranslatable units refuse with a typed reason, go to whoever can act, and are counted by cause.

  + context: Coverage of every translation here is partial.

  + IF:
    A unit cannot be translated under the declared target.

  + HOWEVER:
    Refusal stops work and defaults keep it moving.

  + THEN:
    Refuse typedly, route, and count by cause.

  + BECAUSE:
    Moving on with a substitute gives results about a unit nobody asked about.

  + evidence: :unwarranted handoffs (zai-8 build, 2026-09-16); runtime-correspondence-lagging for P10 (27bfcd3fff); :no-admitted-interpretation (PROPOSAL D1).
